## 12.2 The Buddy Allocator: Physical Page Management

The buddy allocator manages physical memory in power-of-two blocks called *orders*. An order-0 block is a single 4 KiB page; an order-10 block is 4 MiB (1024 pages). When a request comes in for `2^n` pages, the allocator finds the smallest free block of at least that order, and if it is larger, recursively splits it in half, returning the unused half to the free lists.

The core data structure is `struct free_area`, embedded in each `struct page`:

